=== ANGLE 4: transference error = resonance error (framing confirmation) ===
  The dense model (iid residues) = p0_decorr; transference error = |measS7 - dense| = resonance err.
  Already measured <=0.006 at consec base (poserror_consec). So transference IS the wide route,
  not a new mechanism -- it RE-NAMES the resonance error. The Gowers-norm bound on the error
  would be the rigorous version of the 32x-lossy resonance bound.
